. LESSON 2 WRITING MACROS
. Strings go in quotes or brackets. & joins them.
PRINT "HELLO!"

PRINT [HELLO!]

A=[HELLO!]

PRINT A,A,A,A,A

PRINT A&A&A&A&A

. A string of commands is a macro. Typing its name runs it.
Q=[BOX 0,0,100,100,2
BOX 50,50,100,100,3]

P=100
PRINT P
P P
P P 10

. Q would run this too, abbreviated, if it were the only name starting
. with Q. As there is a Q, Q runs that.
QUANTIZED$SECOND$DEGREE$SPACE$INVADERS=[BOX 0,0,100,100,3]

MYBO=BO

ABC=10
DEF=[STRINGYTHINGY]
USEMAP

DEL ABC
USEMAP

. A label starts a line. GOTO jumps to it, and IF runs the rest of its
. line only when its test is true. \ is the remainder of a division.
MANYBOXES=[CLEAR
A=300
10 A=A-3
IF A>0,BOX 0,0,A,A,A\4;GOTO 10]

RANDOMCROSSES=[CLEAR
1MORE X=-160%159
Y=-100%100
LINE X-10,Y,4
LINE X+10,Y,3
LINE X,Y-10,4
LINE X,Y+10,3
GOTO 1MORE]

. THE ANIMATION. TUNNEL draws MANYBOXES's rings again and again, with the
. colors one ring further in each time, so the rings flow inward. A ring
. is drawn as its four sides, not a filled BOX, so each pass recolors
. the rings where they are, and nothing is cleared or flickers. O counts
. 3,2,1,0,3,... so (K+O)\4 never goes negative. Press ESC to stop it.
TUNNEL=[O=0
1PASS K=0;W=300;H=200
1RING C=(K+O)\4;BOX 0,H/2-2,W,4,C;BOX 0,2-H/2,W,4,C;BOX W/2-3,0,6,H,C;BOX 3-W/2,0,6,H,C
W=W-12;H=H-8;IF (K=K+1)<25,GOTO 1RING
O=(O+3)\4;GOTO 1PASS]
TUNNEL
